
Mechanism uniqueness is `1 - structural similarity`. Feasibility requires appropriateness and coherence to meet their configured thresholds. The negative archive is a mechanism-level blacklist; generated candidates are tracked separately in archive cells and the Pareto reservoir.

Niches currently use three dimensions: intervention level, resource intensity, and feedback horizon, producing 36 cells. Coverage is occupied cells divided by 36. Duplicate rate is duplicate attempts divided by valid canonicalized attempts.

Independent niche search and preserving multiple elites reduce premature convergence compared with selecting only one globally highest-scoring idea. Limitations include baseline-relative novelty, illustrative mock assessments, non-semantic hash embeddings, and structural heuristics that cannot prove originality or causal validity.

Provider and embedding protocols are injectable. Production adapters should enforce timeouts, retries, credential isolation, and response validation at their boundary. Seeds and stable identifiers make mock runs reproducible. Generation and total-budget limits bound execution.

Output may be text or JSON, and output files are written through a temporary file followed by an atomic replacement.
